MySQL (SQL - Relational Database)
MySQL is like a strictly structured Excel sheet, where every row must have the same columns.

It stores data in a B+ Tree, which works like a dictionary with sorted pages, making searching efficient.

Uses indexes (B+ Tree) like a table of contents in a book to quickly find information.


